# The drinker split for the discourse-referent experiments. B's witness
# ?x is simulated by the constant x0. Not a form AIDA offers (the author,
# 2026-10-20): A's site under y is the claim itself in y's context, which
# the claim reaches by weakening - A supplies its own omission, and the
# claim's binder captures the site (the hoisting problem). The drinker is
# argued through first-order Peirce instead (drinker_referent.fspy).
lk.
declare Pub : type.
declare c : Pub.
declare x0 : Pub.
declare Dr : Pub -> bool.
# A: first witness c; under the arbitrary y, set Dr y aside as k and owe
# the claim again (right) and its continuation (left).
argument a : (exists x:Pub, Dr [x] -> (forall y:Pub, Dr [y])).
elim [c].
elim h.
elim y.
cut (exists x:Pub, Dr [x] -> (forall y:Pub, Dr [y])) k.
dixi.
# B: second witness, here x0; give up the goal forall y, Dr y (m) and owe
# the context of Dr x0, where d goes.
argument b : (exists x:Pub, Dr [x] -> (forall y:Pub, Dr [y])).
elim [x0].
elim d.
cut (Dr [x0]) m.
axiom d.
dixi.
